 "title": "Ricercar (skeleton) - piano quintet",
 "comment": "Shostakovich Op. 57 model. Quartet alone through the exposition, stretto, Climax I and the arioso dolente (1-34); the alto's lament countersubject dips below the violin (F3, 9:4-12) and goes to the viola while the tenor still rests. The piano enters alone with the inverted fugue (35); the viola brings the stretto entry (37). Over the dominant pedal (42-45) the cello holds the augmented inversion with a piano F1 pedal point under it, and the tenor's S1 entry (44) is the piano's colour. Climax II (46-50) and the apotheosis (51-62) are tutti with octave doublings (piano soprano 8va, bass 8vb).",
